// This file is hand written and is not regenerated by `go generate
// ./internal/ent`: it provides OpenEmbedded, the SQLite shorthand over
// OpenDatabase that a composition root wanting a durable store with zero external
// infrastructure uses, no Postgres, no NATS, just a file on disk.
package ent

import (
	"context"
)

// OpenEmbedded opens an ent Client backed by a real on-disk SQLite file
// at path, applies every pending versioned migration, and returns the
// client ready for use.
//
// It is exactly OpenDatabase against the SQLite adapter, kept as a named
// shorthand because "a file at this path" is a more honest way to ask for
// an embedded database than assembling a DSN, and because the properties
// callers depend on (the parent directory is created, the file is opened
// in WAL mode, migration is idempotent and fails closed) are documented
// on OpenDatabase and its SQLite adapter rather than duplicated here.
//
// Prefer OpenDatabase in a composition root, so that deployment decides the
// backend. Reach for OpenEmbedded when the code genuinely means SQLite
// specifically, which in practice is tests and single-process tooling.
//
// The returned Client must be closed by the caller (Client.Close) once it
// is no longer needed.
func OpenEmbedded(ctx context.Context, path string) (*Client, error) {
	return OpenDatabase(ctx, Config{DSN: sqliteURLScheme + path})
}
